  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The electric field and magnetic field components of an electromagnetic wave going through vacuum is described by</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Then the&nbsp;correct relation between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
